{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:30c14a8a3b13a8ed","name":"Munificent-Class Frigate","source":{"id":"source:reference-30c14a8a3b13a8ed","title":"Munificent-Class Frigate","revision":18757,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:40:53Z","sha256":"96b7b12fa4a991ff6be4159c61a55bb16838b310710408f56e0cfcd6153e7dfe","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18757","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Munificent-Class%20Frigate&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-30c14a8a3b13a8ed","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Confederacy of Independent Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Confederacy_of_Independent_Systems","referenceId":"reference:dfc46c9d666b9b41"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The InterGalactic Banking Clan learned early in its existence that security meant profit. As a result of that philosophy, the clan decided it needed its own communications network separate from ",{"tag":"a","children":["The HoloNet"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_HoloNet"},", and military ships to protect its communications and other investments. The result was the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Munificent"]},"-Class Frigate, a ship so closely associated with the business that custom-ordered its design that it is almost always referred to as the Banking Clan Frigate.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When ",{"tag":"a","children":["San Hill"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/San_Hill?action=edit&redlink=1"}," brought the Banking Clan into the Separatists' fold, he brought the frigates with him. After the defeat of the Confederacy, most of the remaining frigates were scuttled. A few escaped with their crews, becoming pirates or (eventually) members of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebel Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebel_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:52c543ff6d31425c"},". In many cases, the ships were extensively rebuilt by Rebels, radically changing the ships' appearance.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Munificent"]},"-Class Frigates serve as communication ships, troop transports, and front-line ships. In an ideal situation, a frigate could focus on protecting larger ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," and eliminating smaller, more weakly armed ships. Its prow-mounted ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Turbolasers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Turbolasers"}," could punch through the shielding and armor of smaller ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"},", allowing the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Munificent"]},"-Class Frigate to take on military-grade targets. In practice, however, the Banking Clan vessels often had to contend with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Star Destroyers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Star_Destroyers"},"- conflicts that rarely went well for the frigates.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Munificent"]},"-Class Frigate Statistics (CL 18)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal (Cruiser) ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -3; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd